Lindorm Titans inspired the dragons of Viking tales which usually lacked wings, appearing like giant snakes with arms. They were probably based on descriptions of this [[Titan]]. [[Saint George]] was Lindorm's past [[Seeker]] and used [[Sword of Saint George|his sword]] to summon the Titan. {{source|The Treasures of the Argonauts}}

The Titan's Amulet later fell into the hands of [[the Organization]] in the magical Sword of Saint George, but DeFoe's desire for revenge against [[Dante Vale]] made him lose the sword. Lok Lambert eventually managed to bond with Lindorm, although the Titan proved difficult with which to bond, and Lindorm became one of Lok's choice Titans to use in battle. {{source|The Treasures of the Argonauts}} The first time Lindorm was invoked, Lok had no control over the rampaging Titan, yet in a moment of fury, Lok gained perfect control over Lindorm. {{Source|Like Father, Unlike Son}}

Lok used Lindorm to fight a group of [[Suits]] and their [[Titans]] in the [[Newgrange Passage Tomb]]. {{Source|Home Turf}}

In the [[Tomb of Nefertiti]] Lok summoned Lindorm to help the Huntik team fight against [[Klaus]]' Egyptian Suits.  {{Source|The Sceptre Deception}} 

Lindorm was invoked by Lok to fight Rassimov and his Suits in the Amazon Village. Lindorm was later sent back to his amulet because of [[Rassimov]]'s [[Hopeshatter]]. {{Source|Ladies' Choice}} 

When the Legendary Titan of Fate, [[Arc]], became active, Lindorm became [[Powerbonded]] in order to protect Lok. {{source|The Legendary Titan of Fate}}

After being absorbed by Legion, and his Amulet destroyed, Lindorm was trapped within him until Legion's Amulet was destroyed by Lok. This sent Lindorm, as well as all of the other Titans absorbed by Legion, back to [[Spirit World|Huntik]], the spirit world of the Titans. {{Source|Rassimov's Secret}}{{Source|The Spiral Mark}}

[[File:S2E43 Lindorm Harrison.png|thumb|'''Spinscreen''' being used to engulf [[Harrison Fears|Harrison]] in smoke]]
Like other Titans, when the bond between Seeker and the Titan become stronger, Lindorm became Powerbonded Lindorm, obtaining two tails, four arms, four horns on his head, and armor on his body along with the ability to directly communicate with his Seeker. Lindorm's rolling attack became powerful enough to block the [[Legendary Titan]], [[Arc]]. This power, now called '''Spinnerslash''', was now able to be shared with Lok and even powerful enough to knock over a powerful Titan like [[Legion]], Legendary Titan of War. Powerbonded Lindorm tends to act on his own, but he is a strong Titan to have in battle, loyally protecting his Seeker by using his new abilities: 
*'''Spinnerslash''' -  lauches a rolling attack in sync with his Seeker who propels a spinning discs of green energy from their hands. {{source|The Legendary Titan of Fate}}
*'''Spinning Attack''' - launches a rolling charge into his enemies. {{source|The Legendary Titan of Fate}}
*'''Spinscreen''' - traps his enemies in a cloud of smoke. {{Source|Lok's Leadership}}
